{
  "answer": "You can create a custom exception handler in FastAPI by defining a function that takes an exception instance as an argument, and then raising a new exception or returning a response. \n\nFor example:\n```python\nfrom fastapi import FastAPI, HTTPException\n\napp = FastAPI()\n\n@app.exception_handler(HTTPException)\nasync def http_exception_handler(request, exc):\n    return {\"error\": exc.status_code, \"message\": exc.detail}\n```\nThis will catch all HTTP exceptions and return a JSON response with the status code and error message.",
